<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Connect build's network security config: plain http is PERMITTED at the platform level, nothing more.

  Why: cloud sync can send to a WebDAV server on the person's own network (a NAS at http://192.168.x.x),
  and the AI settings already accept a local Ollama at http://127.0.0.1. Android (target 28+) refuses all
  cleartext traffic unless the app says otherwise, so without this those options could never work.

  What it does NOT do: it is not the policy. The policy is in the app's own code. Sync's HttpCaller
  allows plain http only when the person switched "allow plain http" on AND the host is a local address
  (HostRules); the AI client has its own https-or-local check. Anything else in this build that uses
  http:// by mistake would now be sent in the clear instead of failing: Android's per-IP-range scoping
  does not exist (domain-config takes host names, not address ranges), so this cannot be narrowed to
  private networks here. The Offline build has no such file and no network permission at all.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
